# PD emergency lights — no floating orbs

## Hard rule

If a police fleet vehicle already has **native model lamps** (carcols / siren bones) **or** **ELS extras that are physical lamp meshes on the vehicle**, **never** add:

- script `DrawLight` / `DrawMarker` / prop lightbar orbs
- ELS `AllowEnvLight="true"` environmental glow orbs
- copied foreign `carcols` that cast floating coronas away from the model

## How lights must work

| Vehicle type | Mechanism |
|---|---|
| Native Non-ELS (`emergencyLights = 'native'`, e.g. mrpd9–12, mrpd24–26, undercover) | `SetVehicleSiren` + that model's own `carcols` / siren bones only |
| ELS extras (`emergencyLights = 'els'`, e.g. mrpd13–16, mrpd21–23) | ELS toggles **extras on the model**; VCF must use `AllowEnvLight="false"` |
| Civilian + `pd_emergency_kit` only | Script lightbar / DrawLight allowed |

## Do not

- Put Skoda / ELS models on `SetVehicleSiren` with another car's carcols
- Draw script flash for any `Config.FleetVehicles` / `BuiltInFleetModels` / `ElsFleetVehicles` entry
- “Fix” missing lights by adding floating orbs
